<body>

  <h1>Family Module Modular Architecture & Domain Separation</h1>

  <div class="meta-box">
    <strong>Project:</strong> Family Together Sanctuary Backend<br>
    <strong>Module:</strong> <code>src/family/</code> Modular Domain Decomposition<br>
    <strong>Refactoring Target:</strong> Separation of Controllers, Services, and DTOs per Domain<br>
    <strong>Status:</strong> <span class="badge badge-success">Compiled & Verified (Exit 0)</span><br>
    <strong>Runtime Environment:</strong> NestJS 11 + Prisma ORM 7 + PostgreSQL<br>
    <strong>Date of Execution:</strong> September 2026
  </div>

  <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
  <p>
    Previously, <code>family.service.ts</code> was a monolithic file (>42,000 bytes) consolidating the business logic for members, memories, events, documents, invitations, relationships, sanctuary overview, and activity audit streams. Controllers also shared a common query DTO file.
  </p>
  <p>
    This refactoring decomposes the <code>src/family/</code> module into isolated, single-responsibility sub-packages. Each domain feature now resides in its own dedicated directory containing:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Dedicated DTO File:</strong> Contains strongly-typed Request/Response DTOs, Query DTOs (inheriting pagination and search), and class-validator annotations.</li>
    <li><strong>Dedicated Service:</strong> Contains business rules, database transactions, Prisma queries, and external service calls (e.g. <code>MailService</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Dedicated Controller:</strong> Defines routes, role permissions, and OpenAPI Swagger documentation.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>2. Directory Structure Before & After</h2>

  <h3>Before (Monolithic Service & Mixed Files):</h3>
  <pre>
src/family/
├── documents.controller.ts
├── events.controller.ts
├── family.controller.ts
├── family.module.ts
├── family.service.ts       <-- 42,156 bytes (All logic in 1 file!)
├── invitations.controller.ts
├── members.controller.ts
├── memories.controller.ts
├── relationships.controller.ts
└── dto/
    └── family-query.dto.ts
  </pre>

  <h3>After (Modular Domain Decomposition):</h3>
  <pre>
src/family/
├── memories/
│   ├── memories.dto.ts          <-- CreateMemoryDto, UpdateMemoryDto, MemoriesQueryDto
│   ├── memories.service.ts      <-- MemoriesService (privacy isolation, media validation)
│   └── memories.controller.ts   <-- MemoriesController (/family/memories)
├── members/
│   ├── members.dto.ts           <-- CreateMemberDto, UpdateMemberDto, MembersQueryDto
│   ├── members.service.ts       <-- MembersService (directory, user link, deduplication)
│   └── members.controller.ts    <-- MembersController (/family/members)
├── documents/
│   ├── documents.dto.ts         <-- CreateDocumentDto, CreateMultipleDocumentsDto, DocumentsQueryDto
│   ├── documents.service.ts     <-- DocumentsService (encrypted vault, multi-file attachments)
│   └── documents.controller.ts  <-- DocumentsController (/family/documents)
├── events/
│   ├── events.dto.ts            <-- CreateEventDto, EventsQueryDto
│   ├── events.service.ts        <-- EventsService (calendar, virtual gatherings)
│   └── events.controller.ts     <-- EventsController (/family/events)
├── invitations/
│   ├── invitations.dto.ts       <-- CreateInvitationDto, UpdateInvitationStatusDto, InvitationsQueryDto
│   ├── invitations.service.ts   <-- InvitationsService (access requests, email invites)
│   └── invitations.controller.ts<-- InvitationsController (/family/invitations)
├── relationships/
│   ├── relationships.dto.ts     <-- CreateRelationshipDto, RelationshipsQueryDto
│   ├── relationships.service.ts <-- RelationshipsService (graph edges, relation types)
│   └── relationships.controller.ts<-- RelationshipsController (/family/relationships)
├── family.dto.ts                <-- UpdateFamilyDetailsDto, UpdateSanctuarySettingsDto, ActivityQueryDto
├── family.service.ts            <-- FamilyService (Sanctuary stats, audit logs, admin metrics)
├── family.controller.ts         <-- FamilyController (/family/sanctuary, /activity, /settings)
└── family.module.ts             <-- Registers and exports all 7 controllers and services
  </pre>

  <h2>3. Domain Modules Breakdown</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Domain Feature</th>
        <th>Subdirectory</th>
        <th>Service Injected</th>
        <th>Route Prefix</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Memories Vault</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/memories/</code></td>
        <td><code>MemoriesService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family/memories</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Family Members</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/members/</code></td>
        <td><code>MembersService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family/members</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Documents Vault</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/documents/</code></td>
        <td><code>DocumentsService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family/documents</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Family Events</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/events/</code></td>
        <td><code>EventsService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family/events</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Access Invitations</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/invitations/</code></td>
        <td><code>InvitationsService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family/invitations</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Relationships Graph</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/relationships/</code></td>
        <td><code>RelationshipsService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family/relationships</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Sanctuary & Activity</strong></td>
        <td><code>src/family/</code></td>
        <td><code>FamilyService</code></td>
        <td><code>/family</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>4. NestJS ValidationPipe Whitelisting Compliance</h2>
  <div class="callout callout-success">
    <strong>Key Security & Stability Enhancement:</strong> All DTO properties were reinforced with <code>class-validator</code> (e.g. <code>@IsOptional()</code>, <code>@IsString()</code>, <code>@IsBoolean()</code>, <code>@IsArray()</code>). This guarantees compatibility with NestJS's strict <code>ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true })</code>, preventing 400 Bad Request errors on incoming query parameters.
  </div>

